G|0|0|0|0|0|Reconcile(1)>=discrepancy(1,named-skeptic); both connectives accurate/on-tension, no overclaim. Baba verified real: Christopher A. Baba (aka pseudonym "Chris Thiefe"), sole editor of EvilBible.com, and this exact question traces to evilbible.com's "Biblical Contradictions" list per BibViz/philb61 mirror; his KJV "turneth not away for any" quote is exact. Haley 1874 defense verified verbatim on archive.org (examinationofall00hale, p.372): "Man's fear and dread upon all beasts. Not upon the lion... may mean, 'for any beast'... king of beasts... intimidates all the lower animals." defendinginerrancy.com link real, on-topic, on-allowlist, cites Geisler & Howe's When Critics Ask (1992) for the same argument.
